msgstr "Die `Qsettings` _Objektinstanz_"

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "cleanup process"
msgstr "Aufräum-Prozess"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:80
msgid ""
"When QtVCP closes, it calls the *`+_hal_cleanup()+`* function _on all HAL-"
"ified widgets_."
msgstr ""
"Wenn QtVCP geschlossen wird, ruft es die *`+_hal_cleanup()+`* Funktion _auf "
"allen HAL-ifizierten Widgets_ auf."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:82
msgid ""
"The base class creates an empty `+_hal_cleanup()+` function, which can be "
"redefined in the custom widget subclass."
msgstr ""
"Die Basisklasse erstellt eine leere Funktion `+_hal_cleanup()+`, die in der "
"Unterklasse des benutzerdefinierten Widgets neu definiert werden kann."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:84
msgid "This can be used to do such things as record preferences, etc."
msgstr "Damit können Sie z. B. Präferenzen aufzeichnen usw."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:86
msgid ""
"This function is not called when the Qt Designer editor displays the widgets."
msgstr ""
"Diese Funktion wird nicht aufgerufen, wenn der Qt Designer Editor die "
"Widgets anzeigt."

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom HAL Widgets"
msgstr "Benutzerdefinierte HAL-Widgets"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"HAL widgets are the simplest to show example of.\n"
"`qtvcp/widgets/simple_widgets.py` holds many HAL only widgets."
msgstr ""
"HAL-Widgets sind die einfachsten, um ein Beispiel zu zeigen.\n"
"Die Datei `qtvcp/widgets/simple_widgets.py` enthält viele reine HAL-Widgets."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:93
msgid "Lets look at a snippet of `simple_widgets.py`:"
msgstr "Sehen wir uns einen Ausschnitt aus `simple_widgets.py` an:"

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the 'Imports' section"
msgstr "Im Abschnitt \"Imports\""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:96 src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:247
msgid "This is where we import libraries that our widget class needs."
msgstr ""
"Hier importieren wir die Bibliotheken, die unsere Widget-Klasse benötigt."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:108
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"###############################\n"
"# Imports\n"
"###############################\n"
"from PyQt5 import QtWidgets                     # <1>\n"
"from qtvcp.widgets.widget_baseclass \\\n"
"    import _HalWidgetBase, _HalSensitiveBase    # <2>\n"
"import hal                                      # <3>\n"
msgstr ""
"###############################\n"
"# Imports\n"
"###############################\n"
"from PyQt5 import QtWidgets                     # <1>\n"
"from qtvcp.widgets.widget_baseclass \\\n"
"    import _HalWidgetBase, _HalSensitiveBase    # <2>\n"
"import hal                                      # <3>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:111
msgid "In this case we need access to:"
msgstr "In diesem Fall benötigen wir Zugang zu:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:113
msgid "PyQt's QtWidgets library,"
msgstr "Die QtWidgets-Bibliothek von PyQt,"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:114
msgid "LinuxCNC's HAL library, and"
msgstr "LinuxCNCs HAL-Bibliothek, und"

#. TODO explain `_HalToggleBase` and `_HalScaleBase` too
#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"QtVCP's widget `baseclass` 's *`_HalSensitiveBase`* for _automatic HAL pin setup_ and to _disable/enable the widget_ (also known as input sensitivity).\n"
"There is also `_HalToggleBase`, and `_HalScaleBase` functions available in the library.`_HalToggleBase`, and `_HalScaleBase`."
msgstr ""
"QtVCP's widget `baseclass` 's *`_HalSensitiveBase`* für _automatisches HAL-Pin-Setup_ und zum _Deaktivieren/Aktivieren des Widgets_ (auch bekannt als Eingangsempfindlichkeit).\n"
"Es gibt auch `_HalToggleBase`, und `_HalScaleBase` Funktionen in der Bibliothek.`_HalToggleBase`, und `_HalScaleBase`."

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the 'WIDGET' section"
msgstr "Im Abschnitt 'WIDGET'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:122
msgid "Here is a _custom widget_ based on PyQt's *`QGridLayout`* widget."
msgstr ""
"Hier ist ein _angepasstes Widget_ (engl. custom widget), das auf dem "
"*`QGridLayout`* Widget von PyQt basiert."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:124
msgid "`QGridLayout` allows one to:"
msgstr "`QGridLayout` erlaubt es,:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:126
msgid "_Place objects in a grid_ fashion."
msgstr "_Objekte in einem Raster zu positionieren_."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:127
msgid "_Enable/disable all widgets inside it_ based on a *HAL pin state*."
msgstr ""
"_Alle darin enthaltenen Widgets zu aktivieren/deaktivieren_, basierend auf "
"einem *HAL-Pin-Status*."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:133
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"######################\n"
"# WIDGET\n"
"######################\n"
msgstr ""
"######################\n"
"# WIDGET\n"
"######################\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:137
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"class Lcnc_GridLayout(QtWidgets.QWidget, _HalSensitiveBase):    # <1>\n"
"    def __init__(self, parent = None):                          # <2>\n"
"        super(GridLayout, self).__init__(parent)                # <3>\n"
msgstr ""
"class Lcnc_GridLayout(QtWidgets.QWidget, _HalSensitiveBase):    # <1>\n"
"    def __init__(self, parent = None):                          # <2>\n"
"        super(GridLayout, self).__init__(parent)                # <3>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:140
msgid "Line by Line:"
msgstr "Zeile für Zeile:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:149
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This defines the _class name_ and the _libraries it inherits from_.\n"
"This class, named `Lcnc_GridLayout`, inherits the functions of `QWidget` and `+_HalSensitiveBase+`.\n"
"`+_HalSensitiveBase+` is 'subclass' of *`+_HalWidgetBase+`*, the _base class of most QtVCP widgets_, meaning it has all the functions of `+_HalWidgetBase+` plus the functions of `+_HalSensitiveBase+`.\n"
"It adds the function to make the widget be enabled or disabled based on a HAL input BIT pin."
msgstr ""
"Dies definiert den _Klassennamen_ und die _Bibliotheken, von denen sie erbt_.\n"
"Diese Klasse, genannt `Lcnc_GridLayout`, erbt die Funktionen von `QWidget` und `+_HalSensitiveBase+`.\n"
"`+_HalSensitiveBase+` ist eine 'Unterklasse' von *`+_HalWidgetBase+`*, der _Basisklasse der meisten QtVCP-Widgets_, d.h. sie hat alle Funktionen von `+_HalWidgetBase+` plus die Funktionen von `+_HalSensitiveBase+`.\n"
"Sie fügt die Funktion hinzu, um das Widget basierend auf einem HAL-Eingangs-BIT-Pin zu aktivieren oder zu deaktivieren."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:151
msgid ""
"This is the function _called when the widget is first made_ (said "
"instantiated) - this is pretty standard."
msgstr ""
"Dies ist die Funktion, die _aufgerufen wird, wenn das Widget zum ersten Mal "
"erstellt wird_ (d.h. instanziiert wird) - das ist ziemlich standardmäßig."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:155
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This function initializes our widget's *`Super` classes*.\n"
"`Super` just means the _inherited baseclasses_, that is `QWidget` and `_HalSensitiveBase`.\n"
"Pretty standard other than the widget name will change."
msgstr ""
"Diese Funktion initialisiert die *`Super`-Klassen* unseres Widgets.\n"
"Super\" bedeutet einfach die _vererbten Basisklassen_, d.h. `QWidget` und `_HalSensitiveBase`.\n"
"Außer dem Namen des Widgets wird sich nichts ändern."

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom Controller Widgets Using `STATUS`"
msgstr "Benutzerdefinierte Controller-Widgets mit `STATUS`"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:159
msgid ""
"Widget that interact with LinuxCNC's controller are only a little more "
"complicated and they require some _extra libraries_."
msgstr ""
"Widget, die mit LinuxCNC-Controller interagieren sind nur ein wenig "
"komplizierter und sie erfordern einige _extra Bibliotheken_."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:161
msgid ""
"In this cut down example we will add properties that can be changed in Qt "
"Designer."
msgstr ""
"In diesem reduzierten Beispiel werden wir Eigenschaften hinzufügen, die im "
"Qt Designer geändert werden können."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:163
msgid ""
"This LED indicator widget will respond to selectable LinuxCNC controller "
"states."
msgstr ""
"Dieses LED-Anzeige-Widget reagiert auf wählbare Zustände der LinuxCNC-"
"Steuerung."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:177
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"###############################\n"
"# Imports\n"
"###############################\n"
"from PyQt5.QtCore import pyqtProperty\n"
"from qtvcp.widgets.led_widget import LED\n"
"from qtvcp.core import Status\n"
msgstr ""
"###############################\n"
"# Imports\n"
"###############################\n"
"from PyQt5.QtCore import pyqtProperty\n"
"from qtvcp.widgets.led_widget import LED\n"
"from qtvcp.core import Status\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:182 src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:276
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"###########################################\n"
"# **** instantiate libraries section **** #\n"
"###########################################\n"
"STATUS = Status()\n"
msgstr ""
"###########################################\n"
"# **** instantiate libraries section **** #\n"
"###########################################\n"
"STATUS = Status()\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:194
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"##########################################\n"
"# custom widget class definition\n"
"##########################################\n"
"class StateLED(LED):\n"
"    def __init__(self, parent=None):\n"
"        super(StateLED, self).__init__(parent)\n"
"        self.has_hal_pins = False\n"
"        self.setState(False)\n"
"        self.is_estopped = False\n"
"        self.is_on = False\n"
"        self.invert_state = False\n"
msgstr ""
"##########################################\n"
"# custom widget class definition\n"
"##########################################\n"
"class StateLED(LED):\n"
"    def __init__(self, parent=None):\n"
"        super(StateLED, self).__init__(parent)\n"
"        self.has_hal_pins = False\n"
"        self.setState(False)\n"
"        self.is_estopped = False\n"
"        self.is_on = False\n"
"        self.invert_state = False\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:202 src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:322
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    def _hal_init(self):\n"
"        if self.is_estopped:\n"
"            STATUS.connect('state-estop', lambda w:self._flip_state(True))\n"
"            STATUS.connect('state-estop-reset', lambda w:self._flip_state(False))\n"
"        elif self.is_on:\n"
"            STATUS.connect('state-on', lambda w:self._flip_state(True))\n"
"            STATUS.connect('state-off', lambda w:self._flip_state(False))\n"
msgstr ""
"    def _hal_init(self):\n"
"        if self.is_estopped:\n"
"            STATUS.connect('state-estop', lambda w:self._flip_state(True))\n"
"            STATUS.connect('state-estop-reset', lambda w:self._flip_state(False))\n"
"        elif self.is_on:\n"
"            STATUS.connect('state-on', lambda w:self._flip_state(True))\n"
"            STATUS.connect('state-off', lambda w:self._flip_state(False))\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:207 src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:370
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    def _flip_state(self, data):\n"
"            if self.invert_state:\n"
"                data = not data\n"
"            self.change_state(data)\n"
msgstr ""
"    def _flip_state(self, data):\n"
"            if self.invert_state:\n"
"                data = not data\n"
"            self.change_state(data)\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:211 src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:396
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    #########################################################################\n"
"    # Qt Designer properties setter/getters/resetters\n"
"    ########################################################################\n"
msgstr ""
"    #########################################################################\n"
"    # Qt Designer properties setter/getters/resetters\n"
"    ########################################################################\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:219 src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:404
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # invert status\n"
"    def set_invert_state(self, data):\n"
"        self.invert_state = data\n"
"    def get_invert_state(self):\n"
"        return self.invert_state\n"
"    def reset_invert_state(self):\n"
"        self.invert_state = False\n"
msgstr ""
"    # invert status\n"
"    def set_invert_state(self, data):\n"
"        self.invert_state = data\n"
"    def get_invert_state(self):\n"
"        return self.invert_state\n"
"    def reset_invert_state(self):\n"
"        self.invert_state = False\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:227 src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:412
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # machine is estopped status\n"
"    def set_is_estopped(self, data):\n"
"        self.is_estopped = data\n"
"    def get_is_estopped(self):\n"
"        return self.is_estopped\n"
"    def reset_is_estopped(self):\n"
"        self.is_estopped = False\n"
msgstr ""
"    # machine is estopped status\n"
"    def set_is_estopped(self, data):\n"
"        self.is_estopped = data\n"
"    def get_is_estopped(self):\n"
"        return self.is_estopped\n"
"    def reset_is_estopped(self):\n"
"        self.is_estopped = False\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:235 src/gui/qtvcp-custom-widgets.adoc:420
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # machine is on status\n"
"    def set_is_on(self, data):\n"
"        self.is_on = data\n"
"    def get_is_on(self):\n"
"        return self.is_on\n"
"    def reset_is_on(self):\n"
"        self.is_on = False\n"
msgstr ""
"    # machine is on status\n"
"    def set_is_on(self, data):\n"
